    "note": "APPROVE with zero MAJOR. The reviewer independently reproduced the exact 14/12/6 partition with a from-scratch frontmatter splitter (a ::: file also carrying frontmatter counts as frontmatter), ported every validator and ran 60+ adversarial probes with no fail-open across the 32 fixtures. MINOR 1 (a quote inside a %% comment could swallow later statements) was fixed by treating comment lines as inert while outside an open quote, with a regression test. MINOR 2 edge whitelist: the semicolon reject and the requirement that ..> carry : include/extend were applied (both proven corpus-safe); the proposed single-connector count was rejected because a labeled edge A -- \"label\" --> B legitimately has two dash runs, so a chained edge remains an accepted verbatim outline with no incorrect transcription. The unreachable quoted-first-token branch in validate_declaration (NIT) was deleted; anonymous quoted use cases are handled on the raw statement. The conservative classDef/::: prefix gate is inherited byte-identically from the approved architecture/kanban siblings and only forces a safe source fallback. Remaining NITs are zero-corpus-impact C++/Python whitespace tolerances guarded by the drift guard."
